* JACON / RACON draft common LTspice helper models
* These are behavioral/first-order models intended for architecture checks,
* not vendor-accurate S-parameter replacement models.

.param pi=3.141592653589793
.param c0=299792458
.param z0=50

* dBm into 50 ohm -> sine peak voltage.
.func dbm_to_vpk(dbm) sqrt(2*z0*1m*pow(10, dbm/10))

* One-pole low-pass and high-pass approximations.
* Usage:
*   XLP in out lpf_1pole PARAMS: fc=2e9
*   XHP in out hpf_1pole PARAMS: fc=8.4e9
.subckt lpf_1pole in out PARAMS: fc=1e9
Ebuf out 0 LAPLACE {V(in)} {1/(1+s/(2*pi*fc))}
.ends lpf_1pole

.subckt hpf_1pole in out PARAMS: fc=1e9
Ebuf out 0 LAPLACE {V(in)} {(s/(2*pi*fc))/(1+s/(2*pi*fc))}
.ends hpf_1pole

* Voltage gain block with optional soft limiting.
* limit_v=0 disables tanh limiting in practical terms by making the limit huge.
.subckt gain_limit in out PARAMS: gain_db=0 limit_v=1e6
Bout out 0 V={limit_v*tanh(pow(10,gain_db/20)*V(in)/limit_v)}
.ends gain_limit

* Ideal multiplier. Output is scale * Va * Vb.
.subckt ideal_multiplier a b out PARAMS: scale=1
Bmul out 0 V={scale*V(a)*V(b)}
.ends ideal_multiplier

* Behavioral sample-and-hold. Gate > 0.5 tracks input, otherwise holds C.
.subckt sample_hold in gate out PARAMS: ron=10 roff=1e12 chold=100p
Ssh in out gate 0 sw_sample
Chold out 0 {chold}
Rleak out 0 10G
.model sw_sample SW(Ron={ron} Roff={roff} Vt=0.5 Vh=0.05)
.ends sample_hold

* Ideal voltage-controlled oscillator output:
* V(t) = amp * sin(2*pi*(fmin + kvco*V(tune))*time)
* This ignores phase continuity during fast tuning transients; good enough for
* narrow architecture checks.
.subckt simple_vco tune out PARAMS: fmin=1e9 kvco=50e6 amp=0.316
Bvco out 0 V={amp*sin(2*pi*(fmin+kvco*V(tune))*time)}
.ends simple_vco
